menu "py"

config PM_METAL_PY_ENABLE_REPL_SHELL
	bool "Boot straight into the Python REPL shell"
	default y
	help
	  Spawn the cooperative REPL boot shell (pm_metal_py_shell_start) as
	  an async task right after the boot tree prints, before the async
	  runner event loop takes over for good. Wired into
	  boot/platform/private/bringup.c behind
	  CONFIG_PM_METAL_PY_ENABLE_REPL_SHELL (real #ifdef, not a
	  documentation-only toggle).

	  Disable to boot straight to the idle async runner loop with no
	  interactive shell task -- ssh/httpd still serve, UART RX is just
	  never drained.

comment "Heap: py has no private arena -- pm_metal_py_alloc/free/realloc always go through the one shared Metal host heap (pymergetic.metal.mem), sized at bringup by the mem_map arena claim, not by this module. No py-specific heap budget exists here to configure."

comment "REPL buffers (1024B line, 256B feed ring, 64B/step drain) are compile-time Rust consts in py/_loop.rs and py/_shell.rs -- not Kconfig-driven yet (no Rust module reads autoconf.h today)."

comment "DYNAMIC_COMPILER: lexer/parse/compile stay linked in unconditionally today; no frozen-bytecode-only cutdown build exists yet to gate them out of."

endmenu
